window.docContents[206].resolve({"/Hyperbolic-Equations/#PDEAtlas--Hyperbolic-Equations--Symmetric-Systems-and-Conservation-Laws--Conservation-Laws--Scalar-Equations":{"contents":"For  speed and data, the transported datum is a classical solution on\nthe whole strip below the first degeneracy time  of the characteristic\nJacobian, and no  solution extends past . Weak solutions satisfy\nthe distributional identity, with the initial datum entering through a\ntime-zero boundary term or a strong local  trace; entropy solutions add\nthe inequality for every convex entropy pair. For Burgers's equation the\nexplicit Riemann solution is a shock when the left state exceeds the right\nstate and a rarefaction fan otherwise, and it is an entropy solution with the\nstep datum as its strong initial trace.\n\nBeyond Burgers, the scalar theory proves uniqueness twice: in Oleinik's\none-sided class for a convex flux, and for any  flux by the local\n contraction of . For a uniformly convex\nflux the Lax–Oleinik formula gives a weak solution for every bounded datum,\nthe Riemann problem has a\nunique solution in the Oleinik class. Under the stated  flux and\npositive-lobe hypotheses, compactly supported data approach an N-wave at the\nrate  in .\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Hyperbolic Equations\u0009Symmetric Systems and Conservation Laws\u0009Conservation Laws","header":"7.5.2.2. Scalar Equations","id":"/Hyperbolic-Equations/#PDEAtlas--Hyperbolic-Equations--Symmetric-Systems-and-Conservation-Laws--Conservation-Laws--Scalar-Equations"},"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Fourier-Sobolev-Spaces":{"contents":"Fractional and negative regularity can be defined through the Fourier\ntransform. On the whole space the\nFourier transform converts differentiation into multiplication by ,\nso one can ask that  be square integrable for\nany real . This gives a Hilbert scale  of tempered\ndistributions.\n\n\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Sobolev Spaces and Weak Derivatives","header":"4.5. Fourier Sobolev Spaces","id":"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Fourier-Sobolev-Spaces"}});